# DTF tier manifest: conda-hosted-cep16-and-upload  (artifact-keeper#4555 /
#   #4173 encoding half, #4565)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + logging.json-file (the backend's log
# driver pinned so `docker logs` returns every request line).
#
# THE BUGS (both fixed in 1.11.0)
# #4555/#4173  a hosted channel's CEP-16 shard index carried each shard's
#              SHA-256 as a 64-character hex STRING and each shard's records
#              their sha256/md5 as hex strings (the documents were built as
#              serde_json values, which have no byte type), and both were
#              served with `Content-Encoding: zstd` although the zstd frame is
#              part of the `.msgpack.zst` document. rattler's ShardedRepodata /
#              Shard readers expect msgpack `bin` digests and the frame intact.
# #4565        the `http_request` span's `uri` kept the path as sent, so the
#              bearer token in `/conda/t/<token>/<repo>/...` and rattler's
#              `/t/<token>/conda/<repo>/...` was logged in clear.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   GET /conda/{hosted}/noarch/repodata_shards.msgpack.zst, shards/{sha}.msgpack.zst
#       decoded by conda-sharded-remote-virtual/fixtures/cep16.py in a
#       throwaway python:3.14-slim container
#   GET /conda/t/{token}/{hosted}/..., /t/{token}/conda/{hosted}/...
#   docker logs ak-dtf<slot>-backend
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1): see oracle.sh's header.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~15 calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem logging.json-file"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
